const CONTENT_SCHEMA = z.record(z.unknown()).describe(
  "Use schema/relevant kit_authoring_guide sections and per-app vocabulary for custom content; reuse unchanged reads. kit_validate rejects unknown keys. Language needs instructionContent; decision needs decisionSpec, with no commands/whenToUse/resources/memorySetup/selfFactsEnabled. Hybrid needs prose and schema-3 decisionSpec/agentAction; routes agent/escalate/none, source maxItems <=50(default20), agentAction.maxItems <=20(default5), server-gated. Action requires modelType none and explicit actionSpec schemaVersion1 with 1-64 ref/version tools discovered through action_worker_options. No implicit app or kit tool selection. No model/prompts/memory/schedules/triggers/category slots/deployment; omit appCodes/apps, tools derive grants. Invoke via worker_tools/worker_tool_call. Non-Action: appCodes XOR apps, or categorySlots/workerSlots; Language may set apps:[]. Prefer explicit apps: appCodes defaults may grant writes. Review effectivePermissions; prose never narrows grants. MCP uses mcpServers gatewayId/toolIds, not native apps; private API bindings are separate (guide index). One kit installs one worker. workerSlots (max 10) declare portable alias, modelType, operations, required and optional recommendedKit, actionTools or sourceTool/inputFields; never worker/account IDs or keys. Read workers; kit_validate returns exact workerTools schemas/names. Create children separately, deploy hosted children and bind via kit_install.workerBindings or worker_bindings_set; unbound required slots block runs. recommendedKit installs nothing. Contact allow-all is fixed: kits carry no rules. evaluationSpec holds public acceptance criteria, including on protected kits; review with the creator, keep private cases out. Installation copies criteria but never activates quality/learning. See schema for remaining fields."
);

